I agree with geom_rect(), it gets around the geom_bar() < 0 issues mentioned earlier. It's been ages since I've used geom_ribbon() though.

A few layers of geom_rect() and geom_text() or annotate() and you've got 90% of what you want. If you want anyone to spell it out, supply your summary dataset... if you can't supply the original data, make up some data and send that.

